  },
  "question": {
    "text": "The angles <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>C</mi></math> of a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> are in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>.</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then the area (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math>) of this triangle&nbsp;is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;angles&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>C</mi></math> are in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>C</mi></math></p><p>Also, by angle sum property&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#8736;</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Now <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>By, using sine rule, we have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mi>c</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mi>b</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn><mi>&#160;</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#183;</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn><mi>&#160;</mi></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;and hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p>Thus, the triangle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is a right triangle, with hypotenuse&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Again, by Sine rule, we have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0007_1ca1b74f286f.png\" /></p><p>Now, the area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mi>base</mi></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mi>height</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p>"
  }
}